    "tool_results_total": 38,
    "tool_results_with_rtd_marker": 0,
    "root_cause_confirmed_new": "resolveToolClass (brainstem/prime-extension/src/rtd.ts) only ever reads the FIRST non-empty line immediately after the %%bash header as 'the command' -- it never scans further lines. This %%bash cell (correctly, per this machine's own documented PYTHONHOME-pollution workaround) issued three real bash statements: `unset PYTHONHOME`, `unset PYTHONPATH`, THEN the canonical `\"<venv-python>\" -m pytest -vv` invocation the pilot-3-safety-pass resolver was specifically built to recognize. resolveToolClass extracted `unset PYTHONHOME` as the command (first token 'unset'), which is not pytest/git/rg/grep -> eligibility resolved to reason='command' before the size check ever ran, or possibly 'tool' depending on exact branch -- either way RTD never got a chance to evaluate the REAL target command on this multi-statement cell. This is a THIRD distinct, exact root cause across the three real pilots run this campaign (pilot 2: tool-name mismatch, fixed; safety pass: python-path-vs-literal-pytest command-prefix mismatch, fixed for single-statement cells; pilot 3: resolver does not scan past the first bash statement in a multi-statement %%bash cell, not yet fixed) -- not a security concern (this is an eligibility/coverage gap, not an unsafe classification), but a real coverage limitation of the current resolver against a realistic, even AGENTS.md-documented, multi-line bash cell pattern on this machine."
  },
